<https://id.i2idl.org/definitions/transfer-of-training> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "ERIC scope note: The influence that an existing habit, skill, or idea exerts on the acquisition, performance, or relearning of another similar characteristic" <https://id.i2idl.org/graphs/concepts/transfer-of-training/versions/1> .
<https://id.i2idl.org/definitions/transfer-of-training> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://glossarystudio.app/ns/Definition> <https://id.i2idl.org/graphs/concepts/transfer-of-training/versions/1> .
<https://id.i2idl.org/definitions/transfer-of-training> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#value> "The influence of previously acquired knowledge or skills on learning or performing in a subsequent task or context." <https://id.i2idl.org/graphs/concepts/transfer-of-training/versions/1> .
